  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1240 PM CST Thu Nov 19 2026\n\nSW flow aloft will continue over the region as the previously \nmentioned shortwave continues to approach the region. Models show \nthe shortwave moving across the southern Rockies into the region \nover the weekend. Meanwhile, at the surface, a cold front is \nforecast to move across west TX this weekend as well with models \ncurrently showing the front moving into the fa Saturday afternoon or \nearly evening.\n\nThere is a low chance (15-30%) for rain showers in eastern parts of \nthe fa Saturday as the shortwave approaches and begins to move into \nthe region. There is also a low chance for rain, mainly in far NE/E \nparts of the fa, as the cold front moves across the area but most of \nthe activity at that point is expected to be NE and E of the fa. \nAfter this weekend, there is more uncertainty in the models with the \nforecast for next week. Right now, there is a low chance for \nprecipitation (light rain and maybe some light snow) across the fa \nagain on Tuesday as an upper trough moves across the region. \n\nAnother day of mild/warm temperatures is expected on Saturday with \nhighs in the 60s and low 70s. Colder moving into the region behind \nthe cold front will lead to a much cooler day on Sunday with highs \nin the 40s and 50s. These cooler temperatures are expected to \ncontinue next week.\n\nMaxwell",
